To say 'I am ..... years old', you say 'I have ..... year(s)' in Romansh. 

When saying 'I will be ... years old next ...', you don't need to use the future tense, 'Jau hai ... onns l'... proxim(a)' is perfectly correct.

To decribe when you are turning a certain age, if the time adverbial is a word like 'today' or 'tomorrow', put the adverbial *after* 'hai', as in 'jau hai oz indesch onns' means 'today i am turning eleven years old'

To create ordinal numbers, apart from the ones specifically listed in the vicabulary list, all you have to do is add 'avel' to the end of the number